{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "process-evap-permeation-runspec",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.5 step 7d: the `process-evap-permeation` RunSpec computed from the DEFAULT DATABASE. It mounts `moves-onroad.esm` -- the national tables and the onroad model -- and supplies the run's own selections and its expected output.\n\nIT IS THE FIRST RUN HERE THAT NEEDS `TankTemperatureGenerator`, and the generator's four output tables are EMPTY in the default database. `EvaporativePermeationCalculator` multiplies a source-bin-weighted rate by a TANK-TEMPERATURE adjustment (PC-2, `tempAdjustTermA x exp(tempAdjustTermB x averageTankTemperature)` weighted by the evaporative operating-mode distribution) and by an ethanol-bin fuel adjustment (PC-3), and the tank temperature is what the generator computes from the national sample of vehicle trips. On this on-network link the distribution is 0, 0 and 1, so the number that reaches the output is operating mode 300's: the minute-weighted mean tank temperature over every trip segment in hour 7, which depends on every trip and soak earlier in each vehicle's day. The model computes it as one recurrence over `SampleVehicleTrip`'s 37,216 rows with the inner loops closed in algebra (PLAN.md §7.3.31, lib/evaporative.esm), and its six cells here agree with the snapshot's `AverageTankTemperature` to 7.4e-07. Modes 150 and 151 are computed too and multiplied by exactly zero.\n\nWHAT ELSE IT COST THE MODEL. The rate joins read the regulatory class the SOURCE BIN carries for this process, and `sourceTypePolProcess.isRegClassReqd` is 'N' for polProcess 111, so the bins -- and `emissionRateByAge`'s rows -- carry class 0 (docs/evap-permeation.md §0.1, C2'); before `rt_rateRegClassID` every cohort joined no rate and all 64 rows were exactly 0. And `temperatureAdjustment`'s two 111 rows are PC-2a's coefficients, not a quadratic about 75 degF: `BaseRateCalculator`'s S15 would read them as one and multiply every row by 9.281, which is what the first run that emitted numbers did.\n\nIT EMITS 64 ROWS -- 41 gasoline and 23 E85 model years, one block, a rectangle -- and all 64 reproduce at 5.630e-06, the same worst cell the pandas reproduction from the national tables reached before the model changed.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "fixture",
      "onroad",
      "default-database",
      "evaporative"
    ]
  },
  "data_sources": {
    "db_runspecyear": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/process-evap-permeation/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0232_campuscluster_illinois_edu__runspecyear.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_runspecyear"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "scope"
        ],
        "note": "1 row, yearID 2020. The scope comes from these tables and never from the RunSpec XML, whose @key attributes are 0-based indices into sorted ID lists (docs/mixed-onroad.md §0.1).",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_runspecmonth": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/process-evap-permeation/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0232_campuscluster_illinois_edu__runspecmonth.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_runspecmonth"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "scope"
        ],
        "note": "1 row, monthID 8. A key of the thermal chain and not only an axis: TTG-1 starts from `zoneMonthHour` at this month, and the cold-soak tank temperature it produces is every cold trip's key-on temperature and three degrees below where every hot soak ends.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_runspechour": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/process-evap-permeation/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0232_campuscluster_illinois_edu__runspechour.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_runspechour"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "scope"
        ],
        "note": "1 row, hourID 7. The hour TTG-5 averages over: each trip contributes at most one segment and one soak slice to it, because no national trip spans more than 22 hours.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
